WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.040
(audience applauding)
- Welcome to New York.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:02.873
- [Kelly] Thank you.

00:00:02.873 --> 00:00:04.260
- It was such a blast when I
heard you were coming here.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.548
I said, "Maybe we can be on the show-"

00:00:05.548 --> 00:00:06.381
- [Kelly] I know.

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:07.214
and I don't have to go out to LA.

00:00:07.214 --> 00:00:08.047
It's awesome.

00:00:08.047 --> 00:00:09.270
- I know. I love it. I
love coming here too.

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.530
We came here last season.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.480
It opened up premiere week,
and we loved it so much,

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.313
we did it again.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.210
- And the city is really
back in a big way now.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.080
- [Kelly] I know.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.280
You're a music fan, we know this

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.245
'cause you've played music
- I am.

00:00:18.245 --> 00:00:19.078
with us before.
- Yeah.

00:00:19.078 --> 00:00:21.000
- [Kelly] So do you get out?
Do you do shows and all that?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.400
- You know, my band,
we try to get together.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.840
And you know, Covid's been very difficult.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:25.673
We're gonna, I think,

00:00:25.673 --> 00:00:27.360
rehearse in another
week for the first time

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.890
in over a year.
- Oh, wow!

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:29.723
- [Lester] But I love

00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:30.556
live music.
- Mm-hm.

00:00:30.556 --> 00:00:32.130
- I mean, that's part of one
of the gems of New York City,

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.450
is going to hear live music.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.890
- Yeah, and you can hear it everywhere.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.780
Literally, I've spent the whole month here

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:37.950
and I've been in Central Park,

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.500
and everywhere you go there's
a different style of music,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.580
different musicians playing.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.570
It's so cool. Yeah.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.402
- I love street musicians
on the subway, you know.

00:00:44.402 --> 00:00:45.235
- [Kelly] I know.

00:00:45.235 --> 00:00:46.080
- Sometimes you'll be in the subways

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.537
and guys will break out an acapella.

00:00:47.537 --> 00:00:48.540
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.620
- You know, Doo-wop stuff.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.970
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And it's just so cool.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:53.010
- Well, I heard that NBC,
actually, I love this.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.954
They rejected you the first time

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:55.787
(laughing)

00:00:55.787 --> 00:00:57.030
that you wanted to be a
part of the news, right?

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.010
- They did. I just happened,
'cause we talked about this.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.150
I just happened to have a copy.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.140
- [Kelly] I love this.
(audience laughter)

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.070
- A copy-

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.057
- And you, you,
- [Lester] of the letter.

00:01:03.057 --> 00:01:05.490
- you have like 5 billion shows now.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.320
- Okay. This is uh, this is dated.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.420
See, you have the old NBC logo on it.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.960
But anyway, it was from August 11th, 1977.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.940
I was three months out of high school,

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.070
and I sent my, I wanted to be on radio,

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:18.300
I sent my tape and a resume.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.867
Anyway, I get this, "Mr. Lester Holt."

00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:23.040
"Dear Mr. Holt. Thank you
for your interest in WNBC.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.750
I was impressed with your credentials.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.070
However, it's not exactly

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.020
what we're looking for at this time.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.279
Good luck with your career."

00:01:29.279 --> 00:01:30.495
(audience laughing)

00:01:30.495 --> 00:01:31.428
(audience clapping)

00:01:31.428 --> 00:01:32.280
- Good luck?

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.449
- Thank you for that good luck,

00:01:33.449 --> 00:01:34.282
'cause it really, really worked.

00:01:34.282 --> 00:01:36.300
- Oh yeah. I really,
that's amazing though.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.790
And I, I love that you share this story

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.110
'cause a lot of people get deterred.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.090
Like, a lot of people think American Idol

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.130
was my first thing I ever auditioned for.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.630
And I've been turned away from,

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.770
there was like a thing called Popstars

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.300
that got turned away down, down from.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.040
Many things that you get turned down from

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.810
and you have to keep going.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:52.643
- Yeah.

00:01:52.643 --> 00:01:53.476
- [Kelly] I just think
it's such a great story

00:01:53.476 --> 00:01:54.309
for people to hear

00:01:54.309 --> 00:01:56.970
from people like you that
have had so much success.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.560
It wasn't overnight, like it-

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.393
- [Lester] Yeah.

00:01:59.393 --> 00:02:00.720
- You have to keep, there's many doors

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.553
slammed in our faces.
- [Lester] It rarely happens.

00:02:01.553 --> 00:02:02.910
It rarely happens overnight.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:04.320
You just have to have that resilience.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:05.153
That sense of, you know,

00:02:05.153 --> 00:02:07.050
figure out, you know, why.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:08.400
You know, why it was a no and how to

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.803
turn it into a yes next time.

00:02:09.803 --> 00:02:10.993
- [Kelly] Yeah. I love that.

00:02:10.993 --> 00:02:12.203
(audience applauding)

00:02:12.203 --> 00:02:15.480
Well, you just earned a couple big honors.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.590
So, tell everybody about that.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:17.423
That's so cool. It's so cool.

00:02:17.423 --> 00:02:19.500
- Yeah, we won the NBC Overall Excellence,

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.180
the Edward R. Murrow Award.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.070
And also for NBC Nightly News,

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:23.903
which we're incredibly proud of.

00:02:23.903 --> 00:02:24.736
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- [Lester] You know, we work

00:02:24.736 --> 00:02:27.840
really, really hard on
that broadcast every night.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:28.779
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- [Lester] It's, you know,

00:02:28.779 --> 00:02:31.410
we have to bring it and it's
just nice to be recognized,

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:32.820
you know, by your peers,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.370
on that level.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

